MacApp Release 13 Help SummaryHelp information is available for each of the MacApp commands.    To see help information, type    Help -f "{MacApp}"MacApp.Help <command>, e.g.     Help -f "{MacApp}"MacApp.Help Commands      # a list of commands    Help -f "{MacApp}"MacApp.Help MABuild       # MacApp Build System    Help -f "{MacApp}"MacApp.Help Variables     # summary of the standard MacApp® shell variables    Copyright © 1988-1999 by Apple Computer, Inc. All rights reserved.-MABuild          # MacApp Build SystemMABuild [option…] [file…]  ≥ progress    # Default settings are shown in parenthesis following each option's description.    -Asm option…              # Pass through options to Assembler    -BuildFlags               # Get the build flags for these options    -BuildFolder…             # Specify root object folder for this build    -C option…                # Pass through options to C compiler    -CP compiler              # Specify the C++ compiler to use:                              #          MrC, SCpp, MWC68K, MWCPPC                    (SCpp)    -CPlusPlus…               # Pass through generic C++ compiler options    -CreatorAndBundle option… # Pass through options to CreatorAndBundle tool    -d name=(TRUE|FALSE)      # Set compile time variable name in all compilers    -E                        # Pass through -E to Make    -Fat appname              # Build a fat binary by adding the code and resources                              # from a 68K application file    -FolderName               # Get the folder name for these options    -Help                     # Prints this list of options to stdout    -Lib option…              # Pass through options to Librarian    -Link option…             # Pass through options to Linker    -Make option…             # Pass through options to Make    -MakeSYM option…          # Pass through options to MakeSYM    -MrC option…              # Pass through options to Macintosh RISC C/C++ compiler    -MWC68K option…           # Pass through options to Metrowerks C/C++ 68K compiler    -MWCPPC option…           # Pass through options to Metrowerks C/C++ PPC compiler    -MWLink68K option…        # Pass through options to Metrowerks C/C++ 68K linker    -MWLinkPPC option…        # Pass through options to Metrowerks C/C++ PPC linker    -PPCAsm option…           # Pass through options to PPC Assembler    -PPCLib option…           # Pass through options to PPC Librarian    -PPCLink option…          # Pass through options to PPC Linker    -R                        # Pass through -R to Make and write results of Make to stdout    -RAMDisk name             # Use a RAM Disk for pre-compiled headers    -RenameFlag oldname newname  # Rename separate object folders    -Rez option…              # Pass through options to Resource compiler    -RSRC                     # Build only an application's .rsrc file    -S                        # Pass through -S to Make and write results of Make to stdout    -SCpp option…             # Pass through options to the Symantec C++ compiler    -Symantec                 # Equivalent to -CP SCpp (for compatibility)    -Version                  # Display the tool version    -[No]Align                # Longword align all code and data for speed            (Align)    -[No]Attachable           # Support for attaching scripts to objects              (=Delux)    -[No]AutoBuild            # Auto-build the MacApp libraries and any others        (NoAutoBuild)    -[No]Classic              # Build for classic 68K runtime                         (NoClassic)    -[No]Container            # Build as an OpenDoc™ Container application            (NoContainer)    -[No]CPlusLoad            # Make the C++ compiler use load/dump files             (CPlusLoad)    -[No]CreateMake           # Create a make file, even if one already exists        (CreateMake)    -[No]Debug                # Turn on debugging and install debugging gear          (NoDebug)    -[No]DebugMsg             # Turn on extra debugging messages                      (=Debug)    -[No]Delux                # Turn on Attachable, Drag, and PowerTalk               (NoDelux)    -[No]Drag                 # Include support for Drag & Drop                       (=Delux)    -[No]Execute              # Execute the results of Make                           (Execute)    -[No]ExpandEnvVars        # Expand environment vars in AppName.MakeIt             (NoExpandEnvVars)    -[No]Fail                 # Stop executing after first failure                    (NoFail)    -[No]Fast                 # Compile files in one, faster batch                    (NoFast)    -[No]GXPrinting           # Build with support for QuickDraw GX™ Printing         (NoGXPrinting)    -[No]GXViews              # Build with support for QuickDraw GX Views             (NoGXViews)    -[No]Inspector            # Include hooks for the inspector                       (NoInspector)    -[No]LinkMap              # Generate a link map in AppName.map                    (NoLinkMap)    -[No]LinkXRef             # Generate a linker cross reference in AppName.xref     (NoLinkXRef)    -[No]MacApp               # Build for use with MacApp                             (MacApp)    -[No]MALibrary            # Use library, not object files                         (MALibrary)    -[No]ModelCFM             # Build for model CFM-68K support                       (NoModelCFM)    -[No]ModelFar             # Build for model far support                           (NoModelFar)    -[No]ModelFarCode         # Build for model far code support                      (NoModelFarCode)    -[No]ModelFarData         # Build for model far data support                      (NoModelFarData)    -[No]Names                # Include embedded debugging symbols                    (=Debug)    -[No]NeedsColorQD         # Build to require Color QuickDraw™                     (NeedsColorQD)    -[No]NeedsFPU             # Build to require a Floating point unit                (=MrC|MWCPPC)    -[No]NeedsGX              # Build to require QuickDraw GX                         (NoNeedsGX)    -[No]NeedsMC68020         # Build to require a 68020                              (NeedsMC68020)    -[No]NeedsMC68030         # Build to require a 68030                              (=ModelCFM)    -[No]NeedsMC68040         # Build to require a 68040                              (NoNeedsMC68040)    -[No]NeedsSystem7         # Build to require System 7.0 or better                 (NeedsSystem7)    -[No]NeedsSystem7_5       # Build to require System 7.5 or better                 (NoNeedsSystem7_5)    -[No]NeedsVU              # Build for VU compatibility                            (NoNeedsVU)    -[No]P                    # Show progress for the MABuild system                  (NoP)    -[No]Perform              # Include performance monitor code                      (=Debug)    -[No]PP                   # Have all invoked tools show progress too              (NoPP)    -[No]RangeCheck           # Force range/overflow checking                         (=Debug)    -[No]Run                  # Run after build                                       (NoRun)    -[No]Save                 # Auto-save all open windows before starting build      (NoSave)    -[No]SeparateObjects      # Keep separate object folders for each build variation (SeparateObjects)    -[No]SmallSym             # Try to generate smaller symbol files (slow!)          (NoSmallSym)    -[No]StatusOnly           # Write results of Make to stdout                       (NoStatusOnly)    -[No]Sym                  # Generate SADE-compatible symbol information           (=Debug)    -[No]T                    # Show elapsed time for the MABuild system              (NoT)    -[No]TemplateViews        # Include code to create views from templates           (TemplateViews)    -[No]theDebugger          # Support Jasik's The Debugger                          (NotheDebugger)    -[No]TT                   # Have all invoked tools show elapsed time too          (NoTT)    -[No]UserAutoBuild        # Auto-build user-specified libraries {MAUserAutoBuild} (UserAutoBuild)    -[No]Verbose              # Show all kinds of progress for the MABuild system     (NoVerbose)    -[No]WriteTemplateViews   # Include code to write view resources                  (NoWriteTemplateViews)-MABuildFT [option…] [target…]  ≥ progress                              # Use MABuild -cp PPCC                              # or  MABuild -cp MrC-MABuildRSRC [option…] [target…]  ≥ progress                              # Use MABuild -RSRC-CreatorAndBundle [option…] [file…]  ≥ progress    -p                        # write progress information to diagnostic    -t                        # write processing time to diagnostic-Commands    MABuild                   # Build System to compile MacApp® source for 68K    CreatorAndBundle          # Post-process MacApp® applications after Rez.-Variables    Variables defined by the MacApp® Build System startup file:Variables you may want to change:    {MABuildDefaults}           Default options for MABuild.    {MAUserAutoBuild}           List of User targets to automagically build    {MADone}                    Command to run when a build is successful.    {MAFailed}                  Command to run when a build fails.The remaining variables should probably not be changed:Miscellaneous variables:    {MAAutoBuild}               List of MacApp targets to automagically build    {MAAutoBuildPowerPC}        List of MacApp targets to automagically build for PowerPC    {MABuildFlagsExtension}     Filename extension to use for MABuild's buildflags    {MADirectorySeparator}      Character to use for directory separation.    {MAIncludesFolder}          Name for includes folders.    {MALongVersion}             The long version of MacApp.    {MAMakeFileExtension}       Filename extension to use for MABuild "make" files    {MAMakeOutfileExtension}    Filename extension to use for Make's outfile    {MANoSeparateObjectsFolder} Folder name used for NON-Separate objects builds.    {MASeparateObjectsPrefix}   Prefix to put on the folder names generated for                                     Separate objects builds.    {MASetupExtension}          Filename extension to use for MABuild's autoexecute file.    {MAShellVersion}            Version String for MPW.    {MAShortVersion}            The short version of MacApp.    {MASourcesFolder}           Name for source folders.    {MATempFilesExtension}      Filename extension to use for MABuild's tempfiles    {MANoSeparateObjectsFolder} Folder name used for NON-Separate objects builds.Framework library locations:    {MALibraries}               Path to the main MacApp libraries folder.    {MAApp}                     Path to application library.    {MACore}                    Path to core library.    {MADocs}                    Path to document library.    {MAFramework}               Path to framework library.    {MATool}                    Path to MPW tool library.    {MAViews}                   Path to view system library.    {MAODMemMgr}                Path to memory management library.Names and full path of various tools:    {MAAsm}                     Assembler    {MAPPCAsm}                  PowerPC Assembler    {MAC}                       68K C Compiler    {MACPlus}                   68K C++ Compiler    {MAMrCPlus}                 Macintosh RISC C++ Compiler    {MAmwc68K}                  Metrowerks 68K C++ Compiler for MPW    {MAmwcPPC}                  Metrowerks PowerPC C++ Compiler for MPW    {MASCpp}                    Symantec 68K C++ Compiler    {MAEcho}                    Echo command    {MALib}                     68K Librarian    {MALink}                    68K Linker    {MAILink}                   68K Incremental Linker    {MAPPCLink}                 PowerPC Librarian/Linker    {MAMake}                    Make Tool    {MACreatorAndBundle}        CreatorAndBundle Tool    {MARez}                     Resource CompilerMiscellaneous paths:    {MAAsmPaths}                Include paths for the assembler.    {MACPlusIncludes}           Path to the MacApp C Interfaces (if supplied).    {MACPlusPaths}              Include paths for the C++ compiler.    {MADependencies}            Path to the MacApp dependency (partial make) files.    {MAExamples}                Path to the MacApp Example folders.    {MALoadFiles}               Path to use when compilers create load/dump or symbol files.    {MARezPaths}                Include paths for the Rez compiler.    {MARIncludes}               Path to the MacApp Resource Interfaces.    {MAAStructMacs}             Directory to search for structure macros.    {MATemporaries}             Path to use when MABuild creates temporary files.    {MATools}                   Path to the MacApp Tools.